				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;lecture-10-the-evolution-of-smartphone-shapes-and-their-future-development&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Lecture 10: The Evolution of Smartphone Shapes and Their Future Development&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#lecture-10-the-evolution-of-smartphone-shapes-and-their-future-development&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-introduction&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  1. Introduction&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#1-introduction&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The physical shape of mobile phones has changed significantly over the past few decades. From bulky devices with physical keyboards to modern smartphones with large touchscreens, these transformations have been driven by technological development, changing user needs, and improvements in human-computer interaction (HCI).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
